1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:07,620
Mark. Mark 1. The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God.

2
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:10,260
As it is written in Isaiah the prophet,

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:16,240
Behold, I send my messenger before your face, who will prepare your way,

4
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:22,680
the voice of one crying in the wilderness. Prepare the way of the Lord, make his path straight.

5
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:28,040
John appeared, baptizing in the wilderness and proclaiming a baptism of repentance

6
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:34,500
for the forgiveness of sins. And all the country of Judea and all Jerusalem were going out to him

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,620
and were being baptized by him in the river Jordan, confessing their sins.

8
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:44,680
Now John was clothed with camel's hair and wore a leather belt around his waist and ate locusts

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:51,020
and wild honey. And he preached, saying, After me comes he who is mightier than I,

10
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:57,680
the strap of whose sandals I am not worthy to stoop down and untie. I have baptized you with

11
00:00:57,680 --> 00:00:58,020
water.

12
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:01,320
But he will baptize you with the Holy Spirit.

13
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:09,540
In those days Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee and was baptized by John in the Jordan.

14
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:15,360
And when he came up out of the water, immediately he saw the heavens being torn open

15
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:20,780
and the Spirit descending on him like a dove. And a voice came from heaven.

16
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:26,260
You are my beloved Son. With you I am well pleased.

17
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:28,020
The Spirit came from heaven and said,

18
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:33,380
And the Spirit immediately drove him out into the wilderness. And he was in the wilderness forty

19
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:40,340
days being tempted by Satan. And he was with the wild animals, and the angels were ministering to

20
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:47,840
him. Now after John was arrested, Jesus came into Galilee, proclaiming the gospel of God and saying,

21
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:55,820
The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand. Repent and believe in the gospel.

22
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,020
Passing alongside the Spirit, John was baptized with the Holy Spirit, and he was baptized with the

23
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:08,360
Holy Spirit.

24
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:22,400
And he was in God's presence.

25
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,280
And he was in the created one.

26
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,060
In the begotten town, them, who were in the kingdom of God, he was called, and,

27
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:24,440
he called them, and brought them to a ship, and they left their son in the ship.

28
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:24,500
And Moses went away from them, and left them too far away.

29
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,660
And immediately they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired servants,

30
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:28,700
and followed him.

31
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,180
And they went into Capernaum,

32
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,720
and immediately on the Sabbath

33
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,840
he entered the synagogue and was teaching.

34
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,660
And they were astonished at his teaching,

35
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,140
for he taught them as one who had authority

36
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,820
and not as the scribes.

37
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:45,320
And immediately there was in their synagogue

38
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:47,300
a man with an unclean spirit,

39
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:48,800
and he cried out,

40
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:53,840
What have you to do with us, Jesus of Nazareth?

41
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,980
Have you come to destroy us?

42
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:59,600
I know who you are,

43
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,220
the Holy One of God.

44
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:05,120
But Jesus rebuked him, saying,

45
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:08,160
Be silent, and come out of him.

46
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:11,220
And the unclean spirit convulsing him

47
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,580
and crying out with a loud voice came out of him.

48
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,740
And they were all amazed,

49
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:18,360
so that they questioned among themselves, saying,

50
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,780
What is this, a new teaching with authority?

51
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:25,000
He commands even the unclean spirits,

52
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,960
and they obey him.

53
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:30,180
And at once his fame spread everywhere

54
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,800
throughout all the surrounding region of Galilee.

55
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:35,820
And immediately he left the synagogue

56
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:38,240
and entered the house of Simon and Andrew

57
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,440
with James and John.

58
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:42,840
Now Simon's mother-in-law lay ill with a fever,

59
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:45,120
and immediately they told him about her.

60
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,680
And he came and took her by the hand

61
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:50,220
and lifted her up, and the fever left her,

62
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,860
and she began to serve them.

63
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,240
That evening at sundown

64
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,020
they brought to him all who were sick

65
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:57,260
or oppressed by demons.

66
00:03:57,660 --> 00:04:00,540
And the whole city was gathered together at the door.

67
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,460
And he healed many who were sick with various diseases

68
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:05,200
and cast out many demons.

69
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:08,640
And he would not permit the demons to speak

70
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,960
because they knew him.

71
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,880
And rising very early in the morning

72
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,220
while it was still dark,

73
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,060
he departed and went out to a desolate place,

74
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,440
and there he prayed.

75
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:22,780
And Simon and those who were with him searched for him,

76
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,480
and they found him and said to him,

77
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:28,640
And he said to them,

78
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,980
Let us go on to the next towns,

79
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:32,660
that I may preach there also,

80
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,640
for that is why I came out.

81
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:37,060
And he went throughout all Galilee,

82
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,560
preaching in their synagogues and casting out demons.

83
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:41,940
And a leper came to him,

84
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:44,520
imploring him and kneeling, said to him,

85
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:49,120
If you will, you can make me clean.

86
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:52,760
Moved with pity, he stretched out his hand

87
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,460
and touched him and said to him,

88
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,300
I will, be clean.

89
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,340
And immediately the leprosy left him,

90
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,820
and he was made clean.

91
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:05,620
And Jesus sternly charged him and sent him away at once,

92
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:06,640
and said to him,

93
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,960
See that you say nothing to anyone,

94
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,640
but go, show yourself to the priest,

95
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:14,260
and offer for your cleansing what Moses commanded,

96
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:15,700
for a proof to them.

97
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:19,040
But he went out and began to talk freely about it,

98
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,380
and to spread the news,

99
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:23,280
so that Jesus could no longer openly enter a town,

100
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,460
but was out in the city,

101
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:25,360
in desolate places,

102
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,140
and people were coming to him from every quarter.

103
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:30,140
The End

